Algebra (@algebra: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_3TKT81FRMZKC1D63FV1RHY8DCJ
Algebra studies operations, equations, and the structures that organise them. The material progresses from symbolic manipulation to groups, rings, fields, modules, symmetry, and representation, connecting arithmetic and computation with the common structures appearing throughout mathematics and physics.

**First major-branch block developed:** [Foundations, logic and algebraic structure](../foundations-and-structures/Foundations-logic-and-algebraic-structure.lingua) supplies an opening in modular operations and axioms, homomorphisms, compatible equivalences and factorization through the image. Broad group/ring/field/module/representation theory and advanced independent work remain pending.

**Parent:** [Mathematics — quantity, structure, space, change and proof](../Mathematics.lingua#r_0BDE857C410434BA79D017008C).
} r_3TKT81FRMZKC1D63FV1RHY8DCJ
